---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import IconCard from "../components/IconCard.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="For Education"
  active="/education/"
  description="Why AtlasOS is being built for classroom teachers and interactive-board environments."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="For the people in the room"
    title="Built around the classroom day."
    text="AtlasOS is an independent project exploring a practical Live Linux environment for teachers, students, and the teams who support classroom devices."
    image="/AtlasOS/images/atlas-landscape.png"
    imageAlt="Blue layered landscape from the AtlasOS project artwork"
  />
  <section class="page-content">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="content-block">
        <span class="eyebrow">A classroom-minded direction</span><h2>
          Designed for real classroom routines.
        </h2><p>
          The goal is a focused environment that makes common actions easier to
          find while keeping the flexibility of Linux available to technical
          teams.
        </p><div class="feature-grid">
          <IconCard
            icon="▣"
            title="Designed for interactive boards"
            text="The project prioritizes classroom displays and touch-oriented use. Compatibility is still being evaluated across devices."
          /><IconCard
            icon="✦"
            title="Simple for teachers"
            text="A lesson-first home and direct shortcuts aim to reduce the number of steps between starting the system and opening a tool."
          /><IconCard
            icon="◎"
            title="Familiar for students"
            text="A clear, consistent interface is intended to make shared classroom devices easier to approach."
          /><IconCard
            icon="⚙"
            title="Practical for schools"
            text="Linux foundations keep the system understandable for maintenance and future school workflows."
          />
        </div>
      </div><div class="content-block split">
        <div class="visual-card">
          <div class="landscape-card">
            <img
              src="/AtlasOS/images/atlas-landscape.png"
              alt="Blue AtlasOS landscape artwork"
              loading="lazy"
            /><div class="landscape-overlay">
              <h3>Room to learn and explore.</h3><p>
                An independent project for a more focused classroom computing
                experience.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div><div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A better classroom experience</span><h2>
            Useful today, honest about what comes next.
          </h2><p>
            AtlasOS currently provides a Live desktop, teaching-oriented
            shortcuts, and diagnostics tools. An installer, centralized device
            administration, class profiles, offline content delivery, and
            official education-service integration are not established
            capabilities.
          </p><p>
            Physical validation is currently limited to a single owner-reported
            device. The project continues to document what has been tested and
            what remains open.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div><div class="cta-band">
        <div>
          <h2>Follow the work in the open.</h2><p>
            Read the roadmap and source to see how the project is progressing.
          </p>
        </div><a
          class="button button-light"
          href="https://github.com/chavooosss/AtlasOS/blob/main/ROADMAP.md"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer">View the roadmap ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
